# Windows command wording (HTTP examples)

When documenting HTTP command prerequisites or notes for Windows, use a consistent PowerShell-first wording.

## Required wording intent

- State that Windows learners use **`Invoke-RestMethod`** / **`Invoke-WebRequest`** in PowerShell.
- Keep wording self-contained in the lesson itself.

## Do not

- Do not mention **`curl.exe`**.
- Do not mention **Git Bash**.
- Do not reference other lessons in phrasing such as "như các bài trước trong module" / "as in earlier module lessons".
